{"seed":{"mim":"250220","entry_type":"phenotype","prefix":"#","title":"SPONDYLOMETAPHYSEAL DYSPLASIA, SEDAGHATIAN TYPE","alt_titles":["SEDAGHATIAN CHONDRODYSPLASIA","METAPHYSEAL CHONDRODYSPLASIA, CONGENITAL LETHAL"],"symbol":"SMDS","gene_symbols":[],"seed_pmids":[],"max_year":2014},"nodes":[{"id":"entry","type":"Entry","label":"SPONDYLOMETAPHYSEAL DYSPLASIA, SEDAGHATIAN TYPE","mim":"250220","entry_type":"phenotype"},{"id":"section:description","type":"Section","label":"description"},{"id":"section:nomenclature","type":"Section","label":"nomenclature"},{"id":"section:cloning_expression","type":"Section","label":"cloning_expression"},{"id":"section:gene_structure","type":"Section","label":"gene_structure"},{"id":"section:clinical_features","type":"Section","label":"clinical_features"},{"id":"section:other_features","type":"Section","label":"other_features"},{"id":"section:biochemical_features","type":"Section","label":"biochemical_features"},{"id":"section:inheritance","type":"Section","label":"inheritance"},{"id":"section:cytogenetics","type":"Section","label":"cytogenetics"},{"id":"section:mapping","type":"Section","label":"mapping"},{"id":"section:heterogeneity","type":"Section","label":"heterogeneity"},{"id":"section:gene_function","type":"Section","label":"gene_function"},{"id":"section:molecular_genetics","type":"Section","label":"molecular_genetics"},{"id":"section:genotype_phenotype_correlations","type":"Section","label":"genotype_phenotype_correlations"},{"id":"section:pathogenesis","type":"Section","label":"pathogenesis"},{"id":"section:diagnosis","type":"Section","label":"diagnosis"},{"id":"section:clinical_management","type":"Section","label":"clinical_management"},{"id":"section:population_genetics","type":"Section","label":"population_genetics"},{"id":"section:evolution","type":"Section","label":"evolution"},{"id":"section:animal_model","type":"Section","label":"animal_model"},{"id":"section:history","type":"Section","label":"history"},{"id":"paper:24706940","type":"Paper","label":"Smith et al. (2014)","pmid":"24706940","year":2014,"content_level":"abstract","relevance":"primary","title":"Mutations in the enzyme glutathione peroxidase 4 cause Sedaghatian-type spondylometaphyseal dysplasia."},{"id":"paper:22529034","type":"Paper","label":"Aygun et al. (2012)","pmid":"22529034","year":2012,"content_level":"abstract","relevance":"primary","title":"Simplified gyral pattern with cerebellar hypoplasia in Sedaghatian type spondylometaphyseal dysplasia: a clinical report and review of the literature."},{"id":"paper:16892303","type":"Paper","label":"English et al. (2006)","pmid":"16892303","year":2006,"content_level":"abstract","relevance":"primary","title":"Sedaghatian spondylometaphyseal dysplasia with pachygyria and absence of the corpus callosum."},{"id":"paper:10678656","type":"Paper","label":"Koutouby et al. (2000)","pmid":"10678656","year":2000,"content_level":"abstract","relevance":"primary","title":"Spondylometaphyseal dysplasia: Sedaghatian type."},{"id":"paper:9556300","type":"Paper","label":"Elçioglu and Hall (1998)","pmid":"9556300","year":1998,"content_level":"abstract","relevance":"primary","title":"Spondylometaphyseal dysplasia-Sedaghatian type."},{"id":"paper:7211944","type":"Paper","label":"Sedaghatian (1980)","pmid":"7211944","year":1980,"content_level":"abstract","relevance":"primary","title":"Congenital lethal metaphyseal chondrodysplasia: a newly recognized complex autosomal recessive disorder."},{"id":"paper:3565474","type":"Paper","label":"Opitz et al. (1987)","pmid":"3565474","year":1987,"content_level":"abstract","relevance":"primary","title":"Sedaghatian congenital lethal metaphyseal chondrodysplasia--observations in a second Iranian family and histopathological studies."},{"id":"paper:1481828","type":"Paper","label":"Peeden et al. (1992)","pmid":"1481828","year":1992,"content_level":"abstract","relevance":"primary","title":"Spondylometaphyseal dysplasia, Sedaghatian type."},{"id":"finding:7211944:1","type":"Finding","label":"Sedaghatian (1980) reported 2 brothers, born within a year of each other, with a similar skeletal disorder. It consisted of severe congenital metaphyseal involvement, mild rhizomelic shortness of the upper limbs, and mild platyspondyly. Both died at 3 days of age of cardiorespiratory insufficiency.","pmid":"7211944","section":"clinical_features"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0100255","type":"Phenotype","label":"Metaphyseal dysplasia","hpo_id":"HP:0100255"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0004991","type":"Phenotype","label":"Rhizomelic arm shortening","hpo_id":"HP:0004991"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0000926","type":"Phenotype","label":"Platyspondyly","hpo_id":"HP:0000926"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0002093","type":"Phenotype","label":"Respiratory insufficiency","hpo_id":"HP:0002093"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0003811","type":"Phenotype","label":"Neonatal death","hpo_id":"HP:0003811"},{"id":"finding:7211944:2","type":"Finding","label":"Sedaghatian (1980) found that only one of the 2 affected brothers had laboratory tests before death. These showed low calcium, high phosphorus, and high alkaline phosphatase levels, which were attributed to a renal defect.","pmid":"7211944","section":"biochemical_features"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0002901","type":"Phenotype","label":"Hypocalcemia","hpo_id":"HP:0002901"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0002905","type":"Phenotype","label":"Hyperphosphatemia","hpo_id":"HP:0002905"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0003155","type":"Phenotype","label":"Elevated circulating alkaline phosphatase concentration","hpo_id":"HP:0003155"},{"id":"finding:7211944:3","type":"Finding","label":"Sedaghatian (1980) reported that autopsy of the same infant showed pulmonary, renal, and adrenal hemorrhage, along with subendocardial myocarditis and myocardial necrosis. The author stated that the pathogenetic relationship between these manifestations was unclear.","pmid":"7211944","section":"clinical_features"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0040223","type":"Phenotype","label":"Pulmonary hemorrhage","hpo_id":"HP:0040223"},{"id":"phenotext:renal hemorrhage","type":"PhenotypeText","label":"renal hemorrhage"},{"id":"hpo:HP:6001280","type":"Phenotype","label":"Adrenal hemorrhage","hpo_id":"HP:6001280"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0012819","type":"Phenotype","label":"Myocarditis","hpo_id":"HP:0012819"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0001700","type":"Phenotype","label":"Myocardial necrosis","hpo_id":"HP:0001700"},{"id":"finding:7211944:4","type":"Finding","label":"The parents of the affected brothers reported by Sedaghatian (1980) were normal and had recently had an affected baby girl. On this basis the author presumed autosomal recessive inheritance.","pmid":"7211944","section":"inheritance"},{"id":"inh:AR","type":"Inheritance","label":"Autosomal recessive","hpo_id":"HP:0000007"},{"id":"finding:3565474:1","type":"Finding","label":"Opitz et al. (1987) reported another Iranian infant with Sedaghatian syndrome who died on day 4 of life. Histology showed severe epimetaphyseal dysplasia.","pmid":"3565474","section":"clinical_features"},{"id":"phenotext:severe epimetaphyseal dysplasia on histology","type":"PhenotypeText","label":"severe epimetaphyseal dysplasia on histology"},{"id":"finding:3565474:2","type":"Finding","label":"Opitz et al. (1987) summarized Sedaghatian's 1980 report of 2 brothers and a sister with a neonatally lethal disorder marked by slight rhizomelic limb shortening, mild platyspondyly, and severe metaphyseal dysplasia. They suggested the syndrome may be more complexly pleiotropic than the radiographs indicate, because one of Sedaghatian's patients also had microphthalmia, asymmetric ears, depressed nasal bridge, broad nose, short neck, prominent sternum, and short lower extremities.","pmid":"3565474","section":"clinical_features"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0008905","type":"Phenotype","label":"Rhizomelia","hpo_id":"HP:0008905"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0000568","type":"Phenotype","label":"Microphthalmia","hpo_id":"HP:0000568"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0010722","type":"Phenotype","label":"Asymmetry of the ears","hpo_id":"HP:0010722"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0005280","type":"Phenotype","label":"Depressed nasal bridge","hpo_id":"HP:0005280"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0000445","type":"Phenotype","label":"Wide nose","hpo_id":"HP:0000445"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0000470","type":"Phenotype","label":"Short neck","hpo_id":"HP:0000470"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0000768","type":"Phenotype","label":"Pectus carinatum","hpo_id":"HP:0000768"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0006385","type":"Phenotype","label":"Short lower limbs","hpo_id":"HP:0006385"},{"id":"finding:3565474:3","type":"Finding","label":"Opitz et al. (1987) suggested that Sedaghatian syndrome is an autosomal recessive trait with a high gene frequency in Iranians. Their reasons were that children of both sexes were affected in one family, the parents were normal first cousins, and the disorder had so far been seen only in Iranians.","pmid":"3565474","section":"inheritance"},{"id":"finding:1481828:1","type":"Finding","label":"Peeden et al. (1992) reported another infant with spondylometaphyseal dysplasia, Sedaghatian type, who had a lethal course.","pmid":"1481828","section":"clinical_features"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0001522","type":"Phenotype","label":"Death in infancy","hpo_id":"HP:0001522"},{"id":"finding:1481828:2","type":"Finding","label":"Peeden et al. (1992) reviewed the Iranian infant described by Sedaghatian in 1980, who died shortly after birth. At autopsy he had subacute myocarditis, cortical necrosis of the kidneys, and adrenal and pulmonary hemorrhage. His skeletal findings were mild rhizomelic shortening of the limbs, platyspondyly, and 'laciness' of the iliac wings.","pmid":"1481828","section":"clinical_features"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0025418","type":"Phenotype","label":"Renal cortical necrosis","hpo_id":"HP:0025418"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0008786","type":"Phenotype","label":"Iliac crest serration","hpo_id":"HP:0008786"},{"id":"finding:1481828:3","type":"Finding","label":"Peeden et al. (1992) noted that the second reported Iranian infant, described by Opitz et al. in 1987, had a similar perinatal course and similar radiographs. Because this infant was born to first-cousin parents, the authors suggested autosomal recessive inheritance of a single-gene defect.","pmid":"1481828","section":"inheritance"},{"id":"finding:9556300:1","type":"Finding","label":"Elçioglu and Hall (1998) reported the radiological findings in 2 unrelated cases of spondylometaphyseal dysplasia, Sedaghatian type. After reviewing the literature, they identified additional anomalies, including disproportionately long fibulae, dysharmonious maturation, and turricephaly.","pmid":"9556300","section":"clinical_features"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0003085","type":"Phenotype","label":"Long fibula","hpo_id":"HP:0003085"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0000927","type":"Phenotype","label":"Abnormality of skeletal maturation","hpo_id":"HP:0000927"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0000262","type":"Phenotype","label":"Turricephaly","hpo_id":"HP:0000262"},{"id":"finding:10678656:1","type":"Finding","label":"Koutouby et al. (2000) reported an infant with spondylometaphyseal dysplasia born to nonconsanguineous Yemeni parents. The radiologic findings were consistent with lethal metaphyseal chondrodysplasia, Sedaghatian type. All previously reported patients had died within 4 days of life, but this patient survived 161 days.","pmid":"10678656","section":"clinical_features"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0002657","type":"Phenotype","label":"Spondylometaphyseal dysplasia","hpo_id":"HP:0002657"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0005871","type":"Phenotype","label":"Metaphyseal chondrodysplasia","hpo_id":"HP:0005871"},{"id":"finding:10678656:2","type":"Finding","label":"Koutouby et al. (2000) investigated the patient with serum calcium, magnesium, zinc, ammonia, phosphate, alkaline phosphatase and parathormone levels, liver and renal function tests, TORCH, metabolic screening, chromosomal studies, muscle enzymes, EEG, CT scan and brain MRI. Genomic DNA from the patient and parents was analyzed, but no gene abnormality was found.","pmid":"10678656","section":"molecular_genetics"},{"id":"finding:16892303:1","type":"Finding","label":"English et al. (2006) reported a female infant with Sedaghatian spondylometaphyseal dysplasia. She was born to nonconsanguineous Caucasian parents and had a metaphyseal dysplasia. She was hypotonic from birth and had recurrent cyanotic episodes within a few hours of delivery. Brain imaging showed absence of the corpus callosum and marked frontotemporal pachygyria. She developed seizures on day 14 and died at age 17 days.","pmid":"16892303","section":"clinical_features"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0001319","type":"Phenotype","label":"Neonatal hypotonia","hpo_id":"HP:0001319"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0200048","type":"Phenotype","label":"Cyanotic episode","hpo_id":"HP:0200048"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0001274","type":"Phenotype","label":"Agenesis of corpus callosum","hpo_id":"HP:0001274"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0001302","type":"Phenotype","label":"Pachygyria","hpo_id":"HP:0001302"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0001250","type":"Phenotype","label":"Seizure","hpo_id":"HP:0001250"},{"id":"finding:16892303:2","type":"Finding","label":"English et al. (2006) concluded that their case showed neuronal migration abnormalities can occur in Sedaghatian spondylometaphyseal dysplasia. They suggested agenesis of the corpus callosum as a new association of the disorder.","pmid":"16892303","section":"clinical_features"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0002269","type":"Phenotype","label":"Abnormality of neuronal migration","hpo_id":"HP:0002269"},{"id":"finding:22529034:1","type":"Finding","label":"Aygun et al. (2012) reported a patient with Sedaghatian-type spondylometaphyseal dysplasia. The patient had metaphyseal dysplasia, congenital atrioventricular block, a simplified gyral pattern, hypogenesis of the corpus callosum, and severe cerebellar hypoplasia. The authors suggested that central nervous system malformations might be a major component of this congenital lethal skeletal dysplasia and should be evaluated in detail.","pmid":"22529034","section":"clinical_features"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0001678","type":"Phenotype","label":"Atrioventricular block","hpo_id":"HP:0001678"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0009879","type":"Phenotype","label":"Simplified gyral pattern","hpo_id":"HP:0009879"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0002079","type":"Phenotype","label":"Hypoplasia of the corpus callosum","hpo_id":"HP:0002079"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0001321","type":"Phenotype","label":"Cerebellar hypoplasia","hpo_id":"HP:0001321"},{"id":"finding:24706940:1","type":"Finding","label":"Smith et al. (2014) described Sedaghatian-type spondylometaphyseal dysplasia (SSMD) as a neonatal lethal form of spondylometaphyseal dysplasia characterized by severe metaphyseal chondrodysplasia with mild limb shortening, platyspondyly, cardiac conduction defects, and central nervous system abnormalities.","pmid":"24706940","section":"description"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0009826","type":"Phenotype","label":"Limb undergrowth","hpo_id":"HP:0009826"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0031546","type":"Phenotype","label":"Cardiac conduction abnormality","hpo_id":"HP:0031546"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0002011","type":"Phenotype","label":"Morphological central nervous system abnormality","hpo_id":"HP:0002011"},{"id":"finding:24706940:2","type":"Finding","label":"By whole exome sequencing of a girl with SSMD and her unaffected parents, Smith et al. (2014) identified compound heterozygous variants in GPX4 (NM_001039848.1): a maternally inherited c.587+5G>A splice variant, which in vitro studies showed caused splicing out of part of exon 4, resulting in frameshift and premature truncation.","pmid":"24706940","section":"molecular_genetics"},{"id":"gene:GPX4","type":"Gene","label":"GPX4"},{"id":"variant:GPX4:c.587+5G>A","type":"Variant","label":"GPX4 c.587+5G>A","gene":"GPX4","keys":["c.587+5G>A"],"omim_name":"GPX4, 587+5G-A"},{"id":"finding:24706940:3","type":"Finding","label":"In the same girl with SSMD, Smith et al. (2014) identified a de novo GPX4 variant, c.588-8_588-4del (NM_001039848.1), in trans with the maternally inherited c.587+5G>A; in vitro studies showed that it caused skipping of exon 5, resulting in frameshift and premature truncation of GPX4.","pmid":"24706940","section":"molecular_genetics"},{"id":"variant:GPX4:c.588-8_588-4del","type":"Variant","label":"GPX4 c.588-8_588-4del","gene":"GPX4","keys":["c.588-8_588-4del"],"omim_name":"GPX4, 588-8_588-4DEL"},{"id":"finding:24706940:4","type":"Finding","label":"In a second, unrelated child with SSMD whose DNA was not available, Smith et al. (2014) found by Sanger sequencing that both unaffected parents carried the same heterozygous nonsense mutation in exon 3 of GPX4, c.381C>A (p.Tyr127*) (NM_001039848.1).","pmid":"24706940","section":"molecular_genetics"},{"id":"variant:GPX4:c.381C>A","type":"Variant","label":"GPX4 c.381C>A / p.Y127*","gene":"GPX4","keys":["c.381C>A","p.Y127*"],"omim_name":"GPX4, TYR127TER"},{"id":"finding:24706940:5","type":"Finding","label":"Smith et al. (2014) concluded that truncating GPX4 mutations in 2 families with SSMD supported a pathogenic role for GPX4, an antioxidant enzyme that protects cells against membrane lipid peroxidation and is essential for early embryo development. They suggested that their findings highlighted the importance of GPX4 in development of the cardiac, nervous, and skeletal systems.","pmid":"24706940","section":"pathogenesis"}],"edges":[{"src":"paper:7211944","rel":"reports","dst":"finding:7211944:1"},{"src":"finding:7211944:1","rel":"in_section","dst":"section:clinical_features"},{"src":"finding:7211944:1","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0100255","pmid":"7211944","present":true,"frequency":"2/2","text":"severe congenital metaphyseal involvement"},{"src":"finding:7211944:1","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0004991","pmid":"7211944","present":true,"frequency":"2/2","text":"mild rhizomelic shortness of upper limbs"},{"src":"finding:7211944:1","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0000926","pmid":"7211944","present":true,"frequency":"2/2","text":"mild platyspondyly"},{"src":"finding:7211944:1","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0002093","pmid":"7211944","present":true,"frequency":"2/2","text":"cardiorespiratory insufficiency"},{"src":"finding:7211944:1","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0003811","pmid":"7211944","present":true,"frequency":"2/2","text":"death at 3 days"},{"src":"paper:7211944","rel":"reports","dst":"finding:7211944:2"},{"src":"finding:7211944:2","rel":"in_section","dst":"section:biochemical_features"},{"src":"finding:7211944:2","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0002901","pmid":"7211944","present":true,"frequency":"1/1","text":"low calcium"},{"src":"finding:7211944:2","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0002905","pmid":"7211944","present":true,"frequency":"1/1","text":"high phosphorus"},{"src":"finding:7211944:2","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0003155","pmid":"7211944","present":true,"frequency":"1/1","text":"high alkaline phosphatase"},{"src":"paper:7211944","rel":"reports","dst":"finding:7211944:3"},{"src":"finding:7211944:3","rel":"in_section","dst":"section:clinical_features"},{"src":"finding:7211944:3","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0040223","pmid":"7211944","present":true,"frequency":"1/1","text":"pulmonary hemorrhage"},{"src":"finding:7211944:3","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"phenotext:renal hemorrhage","pmid":"7211944","present":true,"frequency":"1/1","text":"renal hemorrhage"},{"src":"finding:7211944:3","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:6001280","pmid":"7211944","present":true,"frequency":"1/1","text":"adrenal hemorrhage"},{"src":"finding:7211944:3","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0012819","pmid":"7211944","present":true,"frequency":"1/1","text":"subendocardial myocarditis"},{"src":"finding:7211944:3","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0001700","pmid":"7211944","present":true,"frequency":"1/1","text":"myocardial necrosis"},{"src":"paper:7211944","rel":"reports","dst":"finding:7211944:4"},{"src":"finding:7211944:4","rel":"in_section","dst":"section:inheritance"},{"src":"finding:7211944:4","rel":"asserts_inheritance","dst":"inh:AR","pmid":"7211944"},{"src":"paper:3565474","rel":"reports","dst":"finding:3565474:1"},{"src":"finding:3565474:1",